    {
      "id": 6,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 6,
        "y": 16,
        "w": 9,
        "h": 8
      },
      "type": "piechart",
      "title": "Trial outcomes  --  $total_trials trials in current session",
      "description": "How the CURRENT session's trials ended. channel is the OUTCOME_* code from task.h: 0 hit, 1 incorrect, 2 no response, 3 abort. Every completed trial is booked under exactly one of them, so the four slices add up to the total in the title.\n\nSession-gated the same way as the rewards gauge beside it (max session_id + start of the local day), so the two always describe the same run. Note this does NOT match the sum of 'Trials per hour', which covers the whole day: the two differ whenever a day has held more than one session.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "postgres",
        "uid": "hathaway_pg"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "postgres",
            "uid": "hathaway_pg"
          },
          "format": "table",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "rawQuery": true,
          "rawSql": "-- One row, one column per outcome: the pie makes a slice of each column.\r\n--\r\n-- Gated to the current session exactly as 'Cumulative rewards (Session)' is:\r\n-- the max session_id, plus the start of the local day. The day bound matters\r\n-- for a session that has run past midnight -- it keeps the pie on today's\r\n-- part of it.\r\n--\r\n-- Filtered on host_ts, not dev_ts: host_ts is indexed and is the hypertable\r\n-- partition key, so Postgres can skip chunks.\r\nSELECT count(*) FILTER (WHERE channel = 0) AS \"hit\",\r\n       count(*) FILTER (WHERE channel = 1) AS \"incorrect\",\r\n       count(*) FILTER (WHERE channel = 2) AS \"no response\",\r\n       count(*) FILTER (WHERE channel = 3) AS \"abort\"\r\n  FROM events_dev,\r\n       (SELECT date_trunc('day', now() AT TIME ZONE 'America/Los_Angeles') AS lm) d\r\n WHERE type = 'OUTCOME'\r\n   AND session_id = (SELECT max(session_id) FROM sessions)\r\n   AND host_ts >= d.lm AT TIME ZONE 'America/Los_Angeles'\r\n   AND host_ts <  (d.lm + interval '1 day') AT TIME ZONE 'America/Los_Angeles'"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic",
            "fixedColor": "#73BF69"
          },
          "custom": {
            "hideFrom": {
              "legend": false,
              "tooltip": false,
              "viz": false
            }
          },
          "unit": "none"
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
